    <allowInChatterGroups>false</allowInChatterGroups>
    <compactLayoutAssignment>SYSTEM</compactLayoutAssignment>
    <deploymentStatus>Deployed</deploymentStatus>
    <description>Generic one-directional favorite/curation junction. A community user can favorite another alumnus (Alumni_Directory__c) or a business listing (Professional_Directory__c). Target_Type__c plus Target_Record_Id__c is used instead of separate lookups per target type so this object can be reused for future alumni connection features without adding more junction objects. Duplicate favorites (same Owner_Contact__c + Target_Type__c + Target_Record_Id__c) are prevented in AlumniFavoriteController Apex, not declaratively - Salesforce does not allow a unique constraint on a formula field, and a plain unique text field would require client-composed keys, which is more failure-prone than an Apex existence check before insert.</description>
    <enableActivities>false</enableActivities>
    <enableBulkApi>true</enableBulkApi>
    <enableFeeds>false</enableFeeds>
    <enableHistory>false</enableHistory>
    <enableLicensing>false</enableLicensing>
    <enableReports>true</enableReports>
